instructions:
Find three examples of Rätoromanisch words or phrases in Graubünden.
The words can be found on:
signs;
public information boards;
place names;
advertisements;
official displays;
or other public sources.

For each word:
take a photo showing the Rätoromanisch word;
guess what it means;
verify the meaning using an available source (for example a sign's explanation, translation information, or another reliable source).

The team must correctly identify the meaning of all three words. If you guess any word wrong, you must find a new one for it to count.

Design your own Freiberger horse profile. Your team must decide:
1) the horse's name;
2) its personality;
3) its special ability;
4) its ideal job;
5) its weakness or funny flaw.

The profile must include at least three real characteristics of the Freiberger breed.
Draw a picture of your horse and make a video (at least 30 seconds long) presenting the profile, then send it to the other team.
You cannot do any research or preparation for this task until you are in canton Jura.

Create a postcard-style photo from three photos of iconic spots within canton Lucerne. You need one photo of each of the following:
1) a lake;
2) at least one mountain;
3) something made by a human.

After taking each photo, verify that the location has a Google rating of at least 4.5 stars. If it does not, find a new one. You cannot research ratings or popular tourist spots on Google beforehand.
Each location must be at least 1km from the others.

Create your own medal ceremony.
Find three objects to represent the medal winners, matched to the correct colours:
gold = first place;
silver = second place;
bronze = third place.

Each object must have a reason why it deserves its medal.
The challenge is complete when the team can explain:
why each object received its medal;
why the gold winner beats the silver and bronze.

Make a video (30 seconds to 1 minute) explaining why you chose each object for gold, silver, and bronze, and send it to the opposing team.

Find 11 different examples connected to the number 11 in Solothurn.
Each example must show the number 11, either written as "11" or represented numerically.
Examples may include:
signs;
buildings;
symbols;
objects;
historical references.

Each 11 you find must be located at least 11 metres from the others.

Take a photo of five different apples in Thurgau. The apples cannot be available for purchase from a supermarket or kiosk.
The apples must have visibly different characteristics, such as:
different colours;
different sizes;
different varieties;
different appearances.

Arrange the apples in a photo from lightest to darkest and send it to the opposing team.

Complete a Zürich public-transport challenge.
The team must travel on four different types of public transport within the canton of Zürich. Possible types include:
1) tram;
2) bus;
3) boat;
4) cog railway;
5) funicular;
6) cable car.

For each type you use, you must:
travel at least 500 metres;
take a photo showing the transport type or vehicle.

The challenge is complete when the team has used four different transport types.
